ype_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Aethersnatch can target any spell, even one without targets.","oracle_id":"45892ec2-8996-444f-a61c-5151926baa0b","published_at":"2015-11-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Combat damage dealt by a commander is tracked without regard to who controlled the commander at the time it dealt damage. For example, say a commander deals 10 combat damage to a player, leaves the battlefield, is recast, and you gain control of it with Aethersnatch. If it deals another 11 combat damage to that same player, they will lose the game.","oracle_id":"45892ec2-8996-444f-a61c-5151926baa0b","published_at":"2015-11-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you gain control of a commander spell, the commander’s owner chooses whether to put it in the command zone if it later leaves the battlefield.","oracle_id":"45892ec2-8996-444f-a61c-5151926baa0b","published_at":"2015-11-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you gain control of an instant or sorcery spell, it will be put into its owner’s graveyard as it resolves.","oracle_id":"45892ec2-8996-444f-a61c-5151926baa0b","published_at":"2015-11-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may change any or none of the spell’s targets. If you change a target, you must choose a legal target for the spell. If you can’t, you must leave the target unchanged (even if the current target is illegal). Notably, if you were originally chosen as a “target opponent” for a spell you gain control with Aethersnatch, you are now an illegal target as you aren’t your own opponent.","oracle_id":"45892ec2-8996-444f-a61c-5151926baa0b","published_at":"2015-11-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Whether you control more creatures than the targeted spell’s controller is checked only as Unified Will resolves. If that player controls more creatures than you at this time, or you each control the same amount, Unified Will simply doesn’t do anything.","oracle_id":"f90cc072-750c-4a87-bf6c-37192d15e691","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
